Photo compressed in-browser via Canvas: resized to max 800px, quality 0.75

Compressed photo converted to base64 and sent in POST

Photo column in Produits tab contains full base64 (long text)

Limit: beyond 20 products with photos, Google Sheets becomes slow; will need external storage (Imgur, Cloudinary)

Problems Encountered and Solutions
CORS: Apps Script doesn't accept POST with Content-Type: application/json. Solution: send as Content-Type: text/plain;charset=utf-8 with mode: 'no-cors'. Consequence: site can't read POST response. To verify a POST worked, check the Sheet, not the site response.

(p.telephone || "").replace is not a function: Google Sheets returns phone numbers as numbers, not text. Solution: convert to string before replace.

javascript
var telephone = String(p.telephone == null ? '' : p.telephone);
var tel = telephone.replace(/[^0-9]/g, '');
ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED, ERR_CONNECTION_CLOSED, ERR_SOCKET_NOT_CONNECTED: Internet connection issues in Burundi interrupting communication with script.google.com. Not a code bug.

Misnamed tabs: Code looked for Vendeurs but tabs were named Vendeur, produit, etc. Solution: rename exactly as in code.

